text:
{
"opening": "This release introduces significant enhancements to the VersionInfo class, including immutability enforcement, iteration support, and new methods for version manipulation. It also adds a command-line interface and utility functions for replacing version components.",
"requirements": [
{
"id": "m04",
"text": "Accessing the major, minor, patch, prerelease, or build attributes of a VersionInfo instance must raise an AttributeError if an attempt is made to modify them."
},
{
"id": "m07",
"text": "A VersionInfo instance must be iterable, yielding its major, minor, patch, prerelease, and build values in that order."
},
{
"id": "m11",
"text": "Comparing a VersionInfo instance with a tuple using standard comparison operators must work correctly, while comparing it with a string or integer must be disallowed."
},
{
"id": "m13",
"text": "The VersionInfo class must provide bump_major, bump_minor, bump_patch, bump_prerelease, and bump_build methods that return a new VersionInfo instance with the respective component incremented."
},
{
"id": "m20",
"text": "When creating a VersionInfo instance, the prerelease and build arguments must be converted to strings, and major, minor, and patch must be integers."
},
{
"id": "m30",
"text": "The module must expose createparser, main, and process functions to support a command-line interface named pysemver."
},
{
"id": "m31",
"text": "The semver module must expose a replace function that takes a version string and keyword arguments to return a new version string, and VersionInfo must have a replace method that returns a new VersionInfo instance."
}
]
}
